WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:02.402
-I have so many things
to ask you.

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:03.570
-Sure.
-But I'm so happy you're here.

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:04.970
-I'm so happy to be back.
-But, first of all,

00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:07.106
even just doing that, I just
want to say congratulations.

00:00:07.106 --> 00:00:09.308
You just got -- You got engaged.
-[ Laughing ] I know.

00:00:09.308 --> 00:00:11.744
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:11.744 --> 00:00:13.879
-Thank you!
-Oh, my gosh, yeah.

00:00:13.879 --> 00:00:15.982
I'm so happy for you, pal.
-Thank you, baby.

00:00:15.982 --> 00:00:17.517
Thank you.
-Now, there's --

00:00:17.517 --> 00:00:19.619
There's been big news, recently.

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:22.121
They announced that
they're making a "Wicked" movie.

00:00:22.121 --> 00:00:26.892
And Ariana Grande got cast to
play Glinda, which is your --

00:00:26.892 --> 00:00:29.962
you made it famous
in the play "Wicked."

00:00:29.962 --> 00:00:31.398
Did you --
Did you talk to Ariana?

00:00:31.398 --> 00:00:34.333
Are you happy with the choice?
-Oh, I couldn't be happier.

00:00:34.333 --> 00:00:36.469
I've known her
since she was 10, y'all.

00:00:36.469 --> 00:00:39.839
She came to the show, and she's
like, "I want to be Glinda,"

00:00:39.839 --> 00:00:42.442
in the same exact voice
that she has now, just like me.

00:00:42.442 --> 00:00:45.812
And I said, "You can be."
And then, her Nana says,

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:48.147
"Oh, you gotta sing for her,"
and she did.

00:00:48.147 --> 00:00:49.615
And she blew me away.
And I was like,

00:00:49.615 --> 00:00:51.250
"You have to have
something of mine."

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:54.553
So, I gave her hand soap
and a fake plastic wand,

00:00:54.553 --> 00:00:56.456
and I said, "Take it."
-Soap?

00:00:56.456 --> 00:00:57.757
-Yes.
-Hand -- Hand soap?

00:00:57.757 --> 00:00:59.892
-I just said, "Take my soap."
I know, it's weird.

00:00:59.892 --> 00:01:01.260
[ Light laughter ]
-Does she remember that?

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:04.530
-Yes. She -- She said, for many
years, she didn't use it.

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:06.866
[ Laughter ]
-Wow.

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:09.602
This is a real photo of you.
-There's --

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:12.404
-And this is
Ariana Grande and -- yeah.

00:01:12.404 --> 00:01:14.807
-And Nana.
-Nonna.

00:01:14.807 --> 00:01:16.542
-And Nonna, right.
-That's right. Nonna.

00:01:16.542 --> 00:01:18.310
Oh, no way.
-Look at her.

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:21.114
-Is that unbelievable, though?
-And now she's playing --

00:01:21.114 --> 00:01:23.916
I'm so happy.
-Isn't that wild how life works?

00:01:23.916 --> 00:01:25.184
That's wild.
-Yes.

00:01:25.184 --> 00:01:27.854
That's when you know
you've been around a second.

00:01:27.854 --> 00:01:29.322
-Oh, no.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:31.457
But, I mean, also, to get the
thumbs-up from you is fantastic.

00:01:31.457 --> 00:01:32.892
Now, the rumors are now,

00:01:32.892 --> 00:01:35.728
are you gonna cameo
in the movie, or would you?

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:37.363
-Well, I haven't
thought about it.

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:38.831
But here's
what I think should happen.

00:01:38.831 --> 00:01:40.899
[ Laughter ]

00:01:40.899 --> 00:01:44.170
So, you know the poster,
how Glinda is always looking --

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:46.506
Yeah, thank you, thank you.
-I'm prepared. Yes.

00:01:46.506 --> 00:01:48.107
-Yes, you are.
And, by the way,

00:01:48.107 --> 00:01:50.309
I begged to have blonde hair
in this, 'cause I feel like

00:01:50.309 --> 00:01:52.278
The Flying Nun,
but that's a separate subject.

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:54.380
[ Laughter ]
I always think --

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:57.283
I just thought it'd be cool
if the camera panned by

00:01:57.283 --> 00:02:00.286
and Idina and I were just there
and we just --

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:03.021
you just saw me go -- yeah.
-[ Imitates whispering ]

00:02:03.021 --> 00:02:04.290
That's a good -- Come on.

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:05.458
That's a good Easter egg,
right there, yeah.

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:06.693
[ Cheers and applause ]
But I want --

00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:08.428
I would want to see
a little bit more of you.

00:02:08.428 --> 00:02:10.129
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:02:10.129 --> 00:02:11.330
-Thanks.
-Because -- yeah.

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:12.998
You know I love you.

00:02:12.998 --> 00:02:14.834
I have a question
I want to ask you about.

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:17.436
-Okay.
-Because we both love him, but,

00:02:17.436 --> 00:02:20.640
I heard that Prince
was a big fan of yours.

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.975
And --
-I -- yes.

00:02:22.975 --> 00:02:25.211
It happened.
I dated him twice.

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:28.081
-You dated Prince?
-I didn't know it was a date,

00:02:28.081 --> 00:02:29.982
because it's Prince.
-Yeah.

00:02:29.982 --> 00:02:31.884
-So, the manager calls me,
and she says,

00:02:31.884 --> 00:02:33.019
"Prince wants
your phone number."

00:02:33.019 --> 00:02:35.088
I was like, "Yeah, right."
[ Snorts ]

00:02:35.088 --> 00:02:37.056
[ Laughter ]

00:02:37.056 --> 00:02:38.757
That's what happened.
-Yeah.

00:02:38.757 --> 00:02:41.961
-And then, Ruth, his assistant,
called me and said,

00:02:41.961 --> 00:02:45.431
"No, Prince, really."
So, I drive in my Honda CR-V

00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:48.267
in L.A. up to -- it was
when he was the symbol.

00:02:48.267 --> 00:02:50.570
-Yeah.
-To the symbol,

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:53.806
and I got through, and there was
a big purple carpet,

00:02:53.806 --> 00:02:57.710
and a waitress there,
and I went in, and the -- the --

00:02:57.710 --> 00:03:00.246
the hallway
was as big as this room.

00:03:00.246 --> 00:03:02.081
And I hear --
I'm in the library,

00:03:02.081 --> 00:03:03.883
and I'm looking at what
Prince is reading, right?

00:03:03.883 --> 00:03:06.185
And I hear, "Click, click,
click, click, click, click."

00:03:06.185 --> 00:03:07.887
-Yeah.
-It's him in his heels

00:03:07.887 --> 00:03:08.954
coming toward me.
-Yes, that's right.

00:03:08.954 --> 00:03:10.289
He wore heels.
Yes, correct.

00:03:10.289 --> 00:03:12.558
-Which was fantastic for me,
because, you know.

00:03:12.558 --> 00:03:16.595
So, he comes in, and I go,
"Hi. I'm --

00:03:16.595 --> 00:03:19.899
I want to party like it's 1999
and ride your raspberry beret."

00:03:19.899 --> 00:03:22.034
-Oh, my God.
[ Cheers ]

00:03:22.034 --> 00:03:24.804
He just was like, "Wah, wah."
-No.

00:03:24.804 --> 00:03:26.873
[ Laughter ]
-And then we -- we had salmon,

00:03:26.873 --> 00:03:29.375
and I hate fish,
and so I put it in my napkin.

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:30.909
[ Laughter ]
-I love these details.

00:03:30.909 --> 00:03:32.478
-Oh, yeah.
I'll never forget, because --

00:03:32.478 --> 00:03:34.146
-What does his -- what did
his place look like?

00:03:34.146 --> 00:03:36.182
-It's -- It's a museum.
-Yeah.

00:03:36.182 --> 00:03:38.017
-It was a museum.
A museum.

00:03:38.017 --> 00:03:41.487
I mean -- then he said, "Do you
want to go see my guitars?"

00:03:41.487 --> 00:03:44.256
I'm like, "No -- Of course!"
-Yes!

00:03:44.256 --> 00:03:47.025
-So we go down to the basement,
which is massive.

00:03:47.025 --> 00:03:50.096
And there's -- y'all,
probably 200 guitars lined up,

00:03:50.096 --> 00:03:52.164
standing there.
And he said, "Pick one up.

00:03:52.164 --> 00:03:54.533
What's your favorite?"
I picked up this white one.

00:03:54.533 --> 00:03:56.002
Picked it up
and start playing a little bit.

00:03:56.002 --> 00:03:57.103
I'm terrible.
And I couldn't believe

00:03:57.103 --> 00:03:59.805
I played in front of him.
I mean, really.

00:03:59.805 --> 00:04:01.173
And I turned it over --
it was really heavy --

00:04:01.173 --> 00:04:03.042
and I go, "What's all this
scratching on the back?"

00:04:03.042 --> 00:04:07.580
He goes, "Elvis's belt."
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:09.748
-Yo! That's a way
to say it, right?

00:04:09.748 --> 00:04:11.917
That's how cool he was.
-Yes, I was practically like..."

00:04:11.917 --> 00:04:13.419
[ Mumbling ]
[ Laughter ]

00:04:13.419 --> 00:04:15.721
I'm passing out, you know?
-Oh, my --

00:04:15.721 --> 00:04:17.924
-I'm so glad I didn't.
But -- yeah.

00:04:17.924 --> 00:04:19.325
-Great story, though.
-Oh, I just couldn't

00:04:19.325 --> 00:04:21.994
believe that he --
Oh, he took me down in the --

00:04:21.994 --> 00:04:23.662
in the basement,
in a movie room,

00:04:23.662 --> 00:04:27.366
and he said, "Watch this."
And he -- I did this opera

00:04:27.366 --> 00:04:29.802
called "Candide" on --
and it was on PBS.

00:04:29.802 --> 00:04:32.705
And he said, "Look at the --
You sing this aria.

00:04:32.705 --> 00:04:35.174
You inspire me."
I'm sorry.

00:04:35.174 --> 00:04:39.178
It's so weird to cry,
but I thought, "Are you insane?

00:04:39.178 --> 00:04:41.146
I'm not watching myself."
And he said,

00:04:41.146 --> 00:04:43.750
"What you do is what
I like to do with the guitar."

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:45.751
And anyway --
-Isn't that unbelievable?

00:04:45.751 --> 00:04:47.253
-Isn't that cool?
-I love that story.

00:04:47.253 --> 00:04:48.387
Thank you
for telling us that story.

00:04:48.387 --> 00:04:49.655
-Of course.
-I appreciate it.

00:04:49.655 --> 00:04:51.324
-I don't tell it very often.
-You know.

00:04:51.324 --> 00:04:53.826
You can always tell --
that means more to me --

00:04:53.826 --> 00:04:55.227
I get it, and I love it.
I appreciate it.

00:04:55.227 --> 00:04:56.762
-Thank you.
I love him.

00:04:56.762 --> 00:04:58.231
-I want to talk to you about
"Happiness is...Christmas!"

00:04:58.231 --> 00:05:00.199
-Oh, right. That.
Right.

00:05:00.199 --> 00:05:02.368
-That's why we --
we got to talk about your album.

00:05:02.368 --> 00:05:05.304
I think this is a great year
to put out a holiday album.

00:05:05.304 --> 00:05:07.006
-They -- They were like,
"What do you want to do?"

00:05:07.006 --> 00:05:08.808
And I said, "I really
want to do a country album."

00:05:08.808 --> 00:05:10.276
And they said,
"No, how about a Christmas?"

00:05:10.276 --> 00:05:12.545
And I wasn't in the mood.
But then I start thinking about

00:05:12.545 --> 00:05:14.713
light -- light at the end
of the tunnel, you know?

00:05:14.713 --> 00:05:16.549
-Yeah.
-And that's why I did it.

00:05:16.549 --> 00:05:17.917
-Yeah. Exactly.
Well, thank you for doing that.

00:05:17.917 --> 00:05:19.185
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:19.185 --> 00:05:22.821
I love you.
Kristin Chenoweth, everybody.

00:05:22.821 --> 00:05:25.058
"Happiness is...Christmas!"
is out now.

